      "writtenOn": "2022-02-18T21:10:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the legacy EC file, correct?\n\nPlease create a bug to track removing this dependency.  You will need declare CHIPSET_STATE_* somewhere in the ap_pwrseq subsystem.\n\nOne idea create a new name-space for these bits, something AP_PWRSEQ_CHIPSET_STATE_*, and then you could have shim/chipset.c code translate the legacy mask bits to the zephyr mask bits.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "fc0cf5e799a0733b3f7934547b7bce01b23a4820",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7655ee59_aabc6007",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/chipset_interface.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 6,
      "author": {
        "id": 1116125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-18T23:59:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not legacy EC header. I changed the name to ap_pwrseq_chipset.h so this will not confused with ec/include/chipset.h.\nI added name space too. Seems I don\u0027t have do the conversion since the enum is passed as int. And the enum here matches what\u0027s defined in ec/include/chipset.h. \n\nAnother change I did is I removed the config guard in shim/src/chipset_api.c. I found out I have to include shim/src/chipset_api.c only when CONFIG_AP_PWRSEQ is set; I can\u0027t just include it because Brya shim zephyr build will be broken. Brya shim zephyr has both HAS_CHIPSET_TASK and CONFIG_ZEPHYR defined. So I have to use CONFIG_AP_PWRSEQ to include shim/src/chipset_api.c, then the config guard inside each API is not needed.",
      "parentUuid": "cd322209_490d1516",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "fc0cf5e799a0733b3f7934547b7bce01b23a4820",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
